<HelpTab>
    <FluentText>Select <strong>Settings</strong> on a kiosk to open its settings. Each tab saves on its own.</FluentText>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>General</strong>: the <strong>Client Name</strong>, and its <strong>Location</strong>. The location
            decides which music schedule it follows, which audio clips and schedules play on it, and which
            opening hours apply. Set it on every kiosk.</li>
        <li><strong>Health</strong>: version, uptime, memory, disk space, audio and DMX devices, projection windows and
            offline readiness.</li>
        <li><strong>Projection</strong>: which program plays on which display, full screen or borderless, and its size.
            Use <strong>Add Projection</strong> to add one.</li>
        <li><strong>Offline</strong>: turn on <strong>Keep screens playing when the server can't be reached</strong>. The kiosk
            keeps a copy of its projection programs and videos and plays them if it loses the server or internet.
            Set how long to wait before switching to offline, and the video cache limit.</li>
        <li><strong>Music</strong>: the <strong>Default Audio Output</strong>. The kiosk checks every minute and switches back
            to it, so a TV or projector that reconnects can't take over the sound. Also the music cache limit.</li>
        <li><strong>DMX</strong>: which DMX device the kiosk sends lighting to.</li>
        <li><strong>Zone Scoreboard</strong>: the network settings for reading the laser game's scores.</li>
        <li><strong>Auto Restart</strong>: restart the PC on a schedule (every so many days or weeks, or monthly, at a set time).</li>
        <li><strong>Updates</strong>: which version the PC runs (see the next tab).</li>
    </ul>
</HelpTab>
